{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"1f0990aaf87ea5500f5d2e1835f219726dc26b3dc3a84dbb683ddfe5d9bb8aba","packTokens":5437,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":5160,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nState, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall let users preview and synchronize supplied mock purchase-order and receiving records, and review the returned source, vendor, cost, head-count, weight, breed, age, and row-outcome information.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The mock procurement and receiving source contains purchase-order and receiving records with available field values. when A user opens the import preview or synchronization results. then The screen displays each returned record's source identifier, vendor, cost, head count, weight, breed, age, source, and row status, as available.\",\n    \"Given A synchronization response contains added, duplicate or already-present, and failed row outcomes. when A user opens the synchronization results. then The screen displays separate added, duplicate or already-present, and failed row counts, and displays the source row and reported failure reason for each failed row.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall let users trace a purchase-order line to one or more lots and lots to pens, and display returned duplicate, pending-mapping, and capacity outcomes while keeping unresolved records unavailable for pen operations.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A purchase-order line is mapped to multiple lots and the lots are assigned to pens. when A user reviews the mapping details and pen view. then The screen displays the source purchase-order line, each linked lot, each assigned pen, and the returned pen capacity and current animal count where available.\",\n    \"Given An import response identifies a duplicate, unmatched record, or row-level problem, or a mapping response refuses an over-capacity assignment. when A user reviews import or mapping results, or attempts the assignment. then The screen displays the affected source row, its returned status and problem detail, and the capacity refusal and limit where applicable; pending records are absent from pen-operation selectors and a refused assignment is not shown as completed.\",\n    \"Given A purchase-order or receiving record has already been imported using its upstream identifier. when A user synchronizes the same records again. then The screen displays the duplicate outcome and does not display a second imported record for that identifier.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall let users view and edit lot target-weight and gain-rate assumptions and display forecasts from incoming animal data, using measured ADG when available and the configured default when it is unavailable.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A lot has incoming animal data, a target weight, and a current measured ADG. when A user opens the lot forecast. then The screen displays the returned target weight, projected market date, and measured gain-rate basis.\",\n    \"Given A lot has no current measured ADG and has a configured default gain rate and target weight. when A user opens the forecast and edits either assumption before requesting a refreshed forecast. then The screen displays the retained submitted assumption values and the forecast response associated with those values, using the configured default gain rate.\",\n    \"Given The forecast response contains a feeding adjustment or sale-timing recommendation. when A user views the lot forecast or insights. then The screen displays the returned recommendation and any associated ADG, projected market date, or plan-variance values supplied with it.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall provide inventory screens to view feed-item details and enter and review stock movements, including separately entered actual wastage.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Inventory responses contain feed items and stock movements. when A user opens inventory details and movement history. then The screen displays each item's name, category, available quantity, unit, unit cost, dry matter percentage, energy value, storage location, and opening, received, consumed, wastage-entered, and closing stock values as available.\",\n    \"Given A user enters actual wastage as a stock movement. when The movement is saved and the user opens the movement history. then The screen displays the returned actual-wastage movement separately from consumption estimates and the configured wastage ratio.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall let users configure a wastage ratio for consumption estimates and projections and review projected inventory balances for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons without low-stock alerts.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A user has configured a wastage ratio and the inventory response contains projected balances. when The user selects each supported forecast horizon. then The screen displays the returned daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual projected balances reflecting the selected ratio in consumption estimates, with each horizon labeled and no low-stock alert shown.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall let users create and view rations with ingredient proportions, nutrition values, intended animal type or weight range, and calculated cost per pound.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A user creates or opens a ration with ingredient and animal-range data. when The ration screen is displayed. then The screen displays the ration name and type, ingredient names and proportions, dry matter percentage, energy value, intended animal type or weight range, and calculated cost per pound.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall compare feasible ration mixes against user-specified nutritional targets or constraints using recorded ingredient costs and nutrition values, and require an explicit user selection before an optimized suggestion is used.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Ingredients have recorded costs and nutrition values and a user submits nutritional targets or constraints. when The user requests ration optimization. then The screen displays returned feasible mixes with ingredient proportions, recorded nutrition values, and costs in lowest-cost order.\",\n    \"Given An optimization suggestion is displayed and the user has not selected it. when The user views the ration workflow. then The screen shows the suggestion as unapplied; after selection, the screen displays the selected ration for use.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall let users generate and review dated feeding plans for specific pens using a selected ration, daily bunk rate, and pen animal count, and display plan status and feeding details.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A pen has an animal count and a user selects a date, ration, and daily bunk rate. when The user generates and opens a feeding plan. then The screen displays the returned plan's date, pen, assigned lot where applicable, animal count, ration, planned quantity, planned feeding time, quantity per animal, total feed cost, expected energy intake, and status.\",\n    \"Given A feeding plan exists for a pen and date. when A user opens that plan. then The screen displays the returned status as Planned, In progress, Completed, or Skipped.\",\n    \"Given A saved plan has actual intake data available. when A user reviews the plan and adjusts it using the displayed intake. then The screen displays planned and actual feed quantities, the variance, and the updated plan value returned after adjustment.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall let users record feeding activities for a pen and date with an optional plan link, and require a separate actual quantity for each affected lot in a multi-lot pen.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A user records a feeding activity for a pen and date where a plan exists. when The activity is saved. then The screen displays the returned plan link, planned and actual quantities, actual-minus-planned variance, feeding status, feed cost, energy value, and inventory consumed.\",\n    \"Given A user records a feeding activity for a pen and date with no plan. when The activity is saved. then The screen displays the returned activity as unplanned and does not require a plan link.\",\n    \"Given A pen contains multiple lots. when The user enters actual quantities for an activity affecting those lots. then The screen requires a separate quantity for each affected lot and displays the returned lot-level quantities.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall display returned feeding-activity costs, energy, inventory consumption, lot consumption, plan variance, and save or shortage outcomes.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A feeding activity is saved successfully and its response contains planned and actual quantities, cost, energy, and inventory consumption. when A user opens the activity details and affected inventory or lot views. then The screen displays the returned feed cost, energy, ingredient consumption, affected lot consumption, and actual-minus-planned variance where a plan exists.\",\n    \"Given The API refuses an activity because available inventory is insufficient. when A user submits the activity. then The screen displays the returned shortage error and does not show the activity as saved.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall let users record, view, edit, and delete lot weight measurements and display the dated measurement series and returned validation or metric updates.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A user records a weight measurement for a lot. when The measurement is saved. then The screen displays the returned measurement date, number of animals weighed, average animal weight, total lot weight, weight gain since the prior measurement, and notes.\",\n    \"Given A lot has multiple saved weight measurements. when A user opens its weight history. then The screen displays the returned readings in date order as a time series, with controls to add, edit, and delete readings.\",\n    \"Given A user edits or deletes a saved weight measurement. when The API returns the updated measurement series, metrics, or a validation error. then The screen displays the returned series and recalculated metric values, or displays the returned error and returned reading-list state without showing an invalid series as saved.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall display returned lot feed-to-gain metrics using applicable headcounts at measurement dates and as-fed pounds for feed conversion, and refresh displayed metrics after feeding or weight events are saved, edited, or deleted.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A lot has a receiving date, feeding events, and weight readings. when A user opens the lot performance view. then The screen displays returned days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total feed consumed, feed conversion ratio, feed cost per pound of gain, and projected ship date.\",\n    \"Given A lot's inventory units require conversion to pounds for feed-to-gain reporting. when A user views performance metrics. then The screen displays total feed consumed in as-fed pounds as the feed conversion ratio basis.\",\n    \"Given The API returns total lot weight gain based on average-weight change and headcount applicable at the measurement dates. when A user views lot performance. then The screen displays the returned total gain and average daily gain values.\",\n    \"Given A feeding or weight event is saved, edited, or deleted and the API returns updated metrics. when A user returns to the affected lot's performance view. then The screen displays the latest returned feed-to-gain metric values without a separate manual recalculation action.\",\n    \"Given A lot's feed cost per pound of gain is displayed. when A user views the metric label. then The screen labels the value as feed cost per pound of gain and does not label it ROI or profitability.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive web app shall provide the public FeedToGainCalculator.calculate method to calculate days on feed, total lot gain, ADG, as-fed feed pounds, FCR, feed cost per pound of gain, and projected market date from supplied receiving, feeding, weight, headcount, and target-weight data.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Calculator input contains receiving and as-of dates, entry and current average weights and applicable headcounts, feeding events with convertible units and costs, and a target weight. when The public FeedToGainCalculator.calculate method is called. then The returned fields contain days on feed as the date difference, total gain as current total lot weight minus entry total lot weight, ADG as total gain divided by days on feed, total feed as feeding quantities converted to as-fed pounds, FCR as feed pounds divided by total gain, cost of gain as feed cost divided by total gain, and projected market date using ADG or the configured default when ADG is unavailable.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall provide lot- and pen-level dashboards showing returned operational and performance metrics, including best- and worst-performing lots.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Dashboard data contains lot, pen, inventory, ration, feeding, weight, and performance data. when A user opens the lot and pen dashboards. then The screen displays active lot and pen counts, animals per lot and pen, inventory status, ration usage, daily bunk rate per pen, planned and actual feed, total feed consumed and cost, starting and current weight, total gain, ADG, FCR, feed cost per unit of gain, energy consumed, and best- and worst-performing lot values with the lots identified.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall provide operational report screens comparing pen consumption, lot performance, ration usage, plan alignment, remaining inventory, and feed cost per unit of weight gain.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The reports response contains pen and lot comparisons. when A user opens an operational report. then The screen displays returned rankings or values for pen feed consumption, lot feed conversion and average daily gain, ration usage, plan alignment, over- or underfeeding, remaining inventory, and feed cost per unit of weight gain.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall provide a feed-to-gain report comparing lot ADG, FCR, and feed cost per pound of gain, with date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters, and use the date range to select the latest weight reading in range and feeding events up to that reading.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The report response contains performance data for multiple lots. when A user opens the feed-to-gain report and applies date-range, breed, sex, or pen filters. then The screen displays the returned filtered lot list and ADG, FCR, and feed-cost-per-pound-of-gain values with the selected date range and filters.\",\n    \"Given A user selects a valid date range, breed, sex, or pen filter. when The user applies the filters. then The screen displays the returned filtered lot list and metric values, with the report date range selecting the latest weight reading in range and feeding events up to that reading.\",\n    \"Given The API refuses an invalid date range or unsupported filter value. when A user applies the filter. then The screen displays the returned error message.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall let users export the filtered feed-to-gain report as a CSV file containing its displayed rows and metrics.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The feed-to-gain report contains filtered lot results. when A user selects CSV export. then The browser downloads a CSV file containing the displayed filtered report rows and ADG, FCR, and feed-cost-per-pound-of-gain fields.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall provide a PDF export action for filtered feed-to-gain report results.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The filtered feed-to-gain report is displayed. when A user selects PDF export. then A downloadable PDF file is produced containing the filtered report rows.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall let users load a clearly labeled, separate demo dataset on demand and display added, already-present, and failed record outcomes without labeling a partial load complete.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A sample dataset is available. when A user opens the sample-data screen. then The screen identifies the dataset as separate demo data and displays an on-demand load control.\",\n    \"Given A sample-data load response reports added, already-present, and failed records, or reports that only some records loaded. when A user reviews the load result. then The screen displays separate counts and record details for added, already-present, and failed data, displays partial-load status where applicable, and does not label a partial load as complete.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall provide a project and demo area presenting the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, an app demonstration, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Project-area content is available. when A user opens the project and demo area. then The page displays the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, app demonstration, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The responsive feedlot web app shall expose the same product areas, operational records, cost and performance views, import screens, and data-entry controls to all users without role-dependent restrictions.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Two users or user contexts open the product areas. when They view operational records, cost and performance views, import screens, and data-entry screens. then The screens display the same available views and operational controls for both users.\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": []\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}